&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You will be Doing&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Staff Test Automation Engineer to lead quality engineering across two high-impact initiatives: our Voice AI, Monitoring &amp;amp; Analytics Platform. In this role you will architect and own the end-to-end test automation strategy, drive quality culture across cross-functional teams, and mentor engineers on best practices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work closely with product engineering, platform, and data teams to embed quality upstream, shifting left from reactive bug-finding to proactive prevention at the architecture level.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Bring to ChargePoint&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and own the overall test automation framework and strategy across both Voice AI and Monitoring &amp;amp; Analytics platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define test pyramid principles - unit, integration, contract, E2E and enforce them across repositories&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead architecture decisions for automation tooling, CI/CD test pipelines, and observability of test health&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish standards for test data management, environment parity, and flakiness elimination&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the performance testing practice - load, stress, soak, and spike testing for backend services and APIs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define performance baselines, SLOs, and regression gates integrated into CI/CD&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Instrument test runs with profiling and APM tooling to identify throughput bottlenecks and latency regressions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build scalable performance test harnesses using Locust, k6, or equivalent frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaboration &amp;amp; Communication:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a technical lead and quality champion, influencing engineering culture, coding standards, and test coverage expectations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor mid-level and senior engineers on automation patterns, code quality, and testing strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with product managers to define acceptance criteria and quality gates at the story level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive root cause analysis on escaped defects and build preventive test coverage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience in software quality engineering with a strong automation focus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record at Staff level, owning QE strategy for complex distributed systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expert-level Python clean, testable, production-grade automation code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with Playwright for E2E browser automation including multi-tab, auth flows, and visual testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep familiarity with FastAPI and Django - understanding of service internals for effective API-level testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience designing and executing performance test programs (load, stress, soak) at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience testing cloud-native platforms on GCP, AWS, or Azure, Kubernetes workloads, managed services, event pipelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with observability stacks: Prometheus, Grafana, OpenTelemetry, or similar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of CI/CD principles and integrating automation into deployment pipelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills, able to present quality strategy to both engineers and executive stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bangalore, India&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
